"([#277](https://github.com/babel/babylon/pull/277)) (Daniel Tschinder)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/parser_CHANGELOG.md:154
msgid ""
"We finally introduce a new compatibility layer for ESTree. To put babylon"
" into ESTree-compatible mode the new plugin `estree` can be enabled. In "
"this mode the parser will output an AST that is compliant to the specs of"
" [ESTree](https://github.com/estree/estree/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/parser_CHANGELOG.md:156
msgid ""
"We highly recommend everyone who uses babylon outside of babel to use "
"this plugin. This will make it much easier for users to switch between "
"different ESTree-compatible parsers. We so far tested several projects "
"with different parsers and exchanged their parser to babylon and in "
"nearly all cases it worked out of the box. Some other estree-compatible "
"parsers include `acorn`, `esprima`, `espree`, `flow-parser`, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/parser_CHANGELOG.md:158
msgid "To enable `estree` mode simply add the plugin in the config:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/parser_CHANGELOG.md:165
msgid ""
"If you want to migrate your project from non-ESTree mode to ESTree, have "
"a look at our [Readme](https://github.com/babel/babylon/#output), where "
"all deviations are mentioned."
msgstr ""

